<https://www.in2use.com/one_earth_bioregions> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                               dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Karl Burkart, One Earth. One Earth Bioregions Framework (Bioregions 2023). Source framework and current Navigator data retrieved 2026-11-10. https://www.oneearth.org/bioregions-2023/"@en ,
                                                                             "RESOLVE Ecoregions 2017 (Dinerstein et al., 2017). Ecoregion-to-biome data accessed through UNEP-WCMC and crosschecked against Esri Living Atlas, 2026-11-10."@en ;
                                               dcterms:created "2026-11-10"^^xsd:date ;
                                               dcterms:creator <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8824-9577> ;
                                               dcterms:description "First draft of the Common Action ontology for One Earth biogeographical regions. Realm divisions, subrealms, bioregions, and ecoregions are represented as geographical individuals; biome categories are represented as individuals of Biome_Type. The updated Big_Bro foundation is incorporated with reused IRIs and logical axioms retained."@en ;
                                               dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/> ;
                                               dcterms:modified "2026-11-10"^^xsd:date ;
                                               dcterms:rights "Ecoregion-to-biome assignments are derived from RESOLVE Ecoregions 2017 data distributed by UNEP-WCMC with a CC BY 4.0 license notice and crosschecked against Esri Living Atlas. The source services and dataset documentation are cited; One Earth names are retained. One documented editorial correction is applied."@en ,
                                                              "The newly authored One Earth-derived ontology content is released under CC BY-NC 4.0. One Earth is the source of the regional framework and source identifiers. The incorporated Big_Bro material retains its Apache License 2.0 terms; the full license text is included in comments at the end of this file. Incorporated SULO material retains its CC0 source notice. Other reused vocabularies retain their applicable source terms. The Big_Bro metadata and source attributions are archived below and do not describe the new ontology itself."@en ;
                                               dcterms:source <https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/server/rest/services/Bio-geographicalRegions/Resolve_Ecoregions/FeatureServer/0/query?where=1%3D1&outFields=eco_id%2Ceco_name%2Cbiome_num%2Cbiome_name%2Crealm%2Clicense&returnGeometry=false&f=json&resultRecordCount=2000> ,
                                                              <https://developers.google.com/earth-engine/datasets/catalog/RESOLVE_ECOREGIONS_2017> ,
                                                              <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mdebellis/Basic_Reusable_Ontology/main/big_bro.ttl> ,
                                                              <https://services.arcgis.com/P3ePLMYs2RVChkJx/arcgis/rest/services/Resolve_Ecoregions/FeatureServer/0> ,
                                                              <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/big_bro> ,
                                                              <https://www.oneearth.org/api/bioregions.json> ,
                                                              <https://www.oneearth.org/api/realms.json> ,
                                                              <https://www.oneearth.org/bioregions-2023/> ;
                                               dcterms:title "one_earth_bioregions"@en ;
                                               vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "oeb" ;
                                               vann:preferredNamespaceUri oeb: ;
                                               rdfs:label "one earth bioregions"@en ;
                                               owl:versionInfo "0.1.0 — first draft" ;
                                               skos:editorialNote "Biome membership joined by numeric ecoregion ID to the RESOLVE 2017 data hosted by UNEP-WCMC and independently crosschecked against Esri Living Atlas. One Earth current ecoregion names are retained. IDs 0 (Rock and Ice), 54, and 400 from the RESOLVE service are absent from the One Earth 844-region set and were not included."@en ,
                                                                  "Ecoregion membership extracted from the public One Earth Navigator JSON for all 185 bioregions on 2026-11-10: 844 distinct ecoregions, 859 membership links. Twelve ecoregions have multiple bioregion associations (eleven mangroves and Campos Rupestres Montane Savanna)."@en ,
                                                                  "Godavari-Krishna Mangroves (316) is assigned to Mangroves based on its One Earth profile, with an explicit note documenting a conflicting RESOLVE biome value."@en ,
                                                                  "Membership assertions follow the structured One Earth Navigator ecoregion lists. Five bioregion summary counts differ from those lists (PA26, PA43, NT14, PA38, NT25); those display counts are not asserted in this ontology. Greater Gobi Desert (PA43) has no structured ecoregion links, and its conflicting prose is documented without inventing assignments."@en ,
                                                                  "Source gap: Greater Gobi Desert (PA43) has an empty ecoregionSet in the One Earth Navigator data. Its page uses the heading Mongolian Desert Steppes and lists ecoregions 824, 825, and 826 in prose, while all three reciprocal ecoregion pages and the structured API associate them with Junggar Semi-Desert & Ermin Valley Steppe (PA38). This unresolved inconsistency is recorded without adding PA43 membership assertions."@en ,
                                                                  "This is an initial draft subject to revision. Source facts were retrieved on 2026-11-10. Geometry, GeoSPARQL execution, political-region instances, and the separate climate-solutions ontology are outside this release. No owl:imports is needed to load the incorporated Big_Bro definitions. No affiliation with or endorsement by One Earth is implied."@en ;
                                               skos:historyNote """Big_Bro source header preserved for attribution and provenance. These are historical source metadata, not the active metadata of one_earth_bioregions.

@prefix : <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/big_bro/> .
@base <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/big_bro/> .


# Big Bro metadata revision: 2026-11-10.
# The original entity definitions and logical axioms below are unchanged.
<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/big_bro> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label \"Big Bro\"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel \"Big Bro\"@en ;
    dcterms:title \"Big Bro - Basic Reusable Ontology\"@en ;
    dcterms:alternative \"Big_Bro\"@en ;
    dcterms:description \"Big Bro is a reusable foundation ontology combining selected Dublin Core Terms and SKOS annotation properties, SULO upper-level classes and relations, and a selected subset of W3C PROV-O. It provides classes and properties for objects, spatial objects, information objects, processes, agents, organizations, locations, time, parthood, participation, and provenance. Reused vocabulary IRIs are retained, together with BRO's existing alignment axioms and annotations.\"@en ;
    rdfs:comment \"Big Bro is the middle layer of the Basic Reusable Ontology (BRO) family. This Turtle file contains the reused term definitions directly and has no owl:imports declarations.\"@en ;
    dcterms:creator <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8824-9577> ;
    dcterms:modified \"2026-11-10\"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
    dcterms:license <https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0> ;
    dcterms:rights \"Big Bro is distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, as stated in the Basic_Reusable_Ontology repository LICENSE. The incorporated SULO source is published under CC0 1.0. Reused vocabulary content retains its applicable source terms and attribution; the complete prior header, including source notices and credits, is preserved in skos:historyNote.\"@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://w3id.org/sulo/>,
        <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov-o>,
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>,
        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core> ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix \"big_bro\" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri <https://www.michaeldebellis.com/big_bro/> ;
    foaf:homepage <https://github.com/mdebellis/Basic_Reusable_Ontology> ;
    dcat:accessURL <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mdebellis/Basic_Reusable_Ontology/main/big_bro.ttl> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/sulo/>,
        <https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/>,
        <https://github.com/mdebellis/Basic_Reusable_Ontology/blob/main/README.md> ;
    owl:versionInfo \"2026-11-10 metadata revision\" ;
    skos:editorialNote \"Use dcterms:* for new Dublin Core metadata. The legacy dc:creator declaration is retained for compatibility with the existing vocabulary. Reused SULO, PROV, SKOS, and Dublin Core IRIs are preserved.\"@en ;
    skos:note \"SULO source attribution: Michel Dumontier, Remzi Çelebi, Komal Gilani, Isabelle de Zegher, Katerina Serafimova, Catalina Martínez Costa and Stefan Schulz. SULO - a simplified upper-level ontology. Proceedings of the Joint Ontology Workshops (JOWO) - Episode XI: The Sicilian Summer under the Etna, co-located with the 15th International Conference on Formal Ontology in Information Systems (FOIS 2025), September 8-9, 2025, Catania, Italy. Original author identifiers and funding attribution are preserved in skos:historyNote.\"@en ;
    mod:definitionProperty rdfs:comment ;
    mod:hasRepresentationLanguage <http://omv.ontoware.org/2005/05/ontology#OWL> ;
    mod:hasSyntax <http://www.w3.org/ns/formats/Turtle> ;
    mod:prefLabelProperty rdfs:label ;
    mod:status \"active\" ;
    skos:changeNote \"2026-11-10: Corrected ontology-level metadata for Big Bro. Replaced the metadata-only Basic Bro description; corrected the creator, namespace metadata, homepage, and access URL; scoped the ontology license to Apache 2.0 in accordance with the BRO repository LICENSE; identified the CC0 notice as applying to the incorporated SULO source; removed inherited SULO release, compatibility, catalog, funding, and publication-date assertions from active Big Bro metadata; preserved the complete previous header in skos:historyNote. No entity IRIs, entity annotations, class axioms, property axioms, or instance assertions were changed.\"@en,
        \"\"\"2025-11-29 (M. DeBellis): Created PROV-Lite as a cleaned subset of the W3C PROV-O Turtle serialization for use with the Basic Reusable Ontology (Big Bro).
– Removed duplicate owl:Ontology declarations.
– Moved orphaned ontology metadata triples (label, seeAlso, versionIRI, versionInfo, specializationOf, wasRevisionOf) under this ontology IRI.
– Removed stray non-comment prose that appeared after the :wasStartedBy axiom and caused Turtle parse errors.
– Trimmed PROV terms and axioms not required by Big Bro, without changing the IRIs or logical meaning of the retained PROV terms.\"\"\"@en,
        \"\"\"Imported SULO upper model: https://w3id.org/sulo/
December 17, 2025
Michael DeBellis\"\"\" ;
    skos:historyNote \"\"\"Historical ontology header, preserved verbatim from the source file before the metadata cleanup on 2026-11-10. This record combines earlier Big Bro, Basic Bro, SULO, and PROV-Lite metadata; the claims below are historical and are not the current metadata of Big Bro. Source at retrieval: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mdebellis/Basic_Reusable_Ontology/main/big_bro.ttl

<https://www.michaeldebellis.com/big_bro> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4727-9435> ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/alternative> \"SULO\"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> \"Michel Dumontier, Remzi Çelebi, Komal Gilani, Isabelle de Zegher, Katerina Serafimova, Catalina Martínez Costa and Stefan Schulz. SULO - a simplified upper-level ontology. Proceedings of the Joint Ontology Workshops (JOWO) - Episode XI: The Sicilian Summer under the Etna, co-located with the 15th International Conference on Formal Ontology in Information Systems (FOIS 2025), September 8-9, 2025, Catania, Italy\"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7222-3287> ,
                                                                                  \"Michael DeBellis Orcid ID: 0000-0002-8824-9577\"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> \"2024-11-11\" ,
                                                                              \"2025-28-11\" ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> \"Basic_Bro  provides core metadata annotation properties by reusing SKOS and DCTERMS. It is the foundational module used by all BRO layers and includes only annotation and datatype properties, with no classes or object properties.\"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> \"2025-07-11\" ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/language> <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-1/en> ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0> ,
                                                                              <https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0> ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> \"2026-05-19\" ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4727-9435> ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> \"Basic Reusable Ontology 1 big_bro\"@en ,
                                                                            \"Simplified Upper Level Ontology\"@en ;
                                           <http://purl.org/pav/authoredBy> <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4727-9435> ;
                                           <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> \"sulo\" ;
                                           <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> <https://w3id.org/sulo/> ;
                                           rdfs:comment \"Subset of the W3C PROV-O ontology containing only the terms needed by the Basic Reusable Ontology (Big Bro). IRIs of PROV terms are preserved; content not required by Big Bro has been omitted.\"@en ,
                                                        \"The Simplified Upper Level Ontology (SULO) is ontology with a minimal set of classes and relations to guide the development of a personal health knowledge graph.\"@en ;
                                           rdfs:label \"Big Bro\"@en ;
                                           rdfs:seeAlso <http://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/> ,
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov> ;
                                           owl:backwardCompatibleWith <https://w3id.org/sulo/sulo-0.2.3.ttl> ;
                                           owl:priorVersion <https://w3id.org/sulo/sulo-0.2.3.ttl> ;
                                           owl:versionInfo \"Recommendation version 2013-04-30, subsetted as PROV-Lite for Big Bro\"@en ,
                                                           \"0.2.14\" ,
                                                           \"1.0.0\" ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> \\\"\\\"\\\"2025-11-29 (M. DeBellis): Created PROV-Lite as a cleaned subset of the W3C PROV-O Turtle serialization for use with the Basic Reusable Ontology (Big Bro).
– Removed duplicate owl:Ontology declarations.
– Moved orphaned ontology metadata triples (label, seeAlso, versionIRI, versionInfo, specializationOf, wasRevisionOf) under this ontology IRI.
– Removed stray non-comment prose that appeared after the :wasStartedBy axiom and caused Turtle parse errors.
– Trimmed PROV terms and axioms not required by Big Bro, without changing the IRIs or logical meaning of the retained PROV terms.\\\"\\\"\\\"@en ,
                                                                                            \\\"\\\"\\\"Imported SULO upper model: https://w3id.org/sulo/
December 17, 2025
Michael DeBellis\\\"\\\"\\\" ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> \"Basic_Bro includes the legacy Dublin Core (dc:) namespace only because it is automatically imported by DCTERMS for backward compatibility. BRO users should always use dcterms:* properties and never use dc:* properties.\"@en ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> \"Basic_Bro reuses annotation and datatype properties from the SKOS and DCTERMS vocabularies. All classes and object properties from imported vocabularies have been removed to provide a clean metadata-only reusable layer.\"@en ;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#accessURL> <https://w3id.org/sulo/sulo.ttl> ;
                                           <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/homepage> <https://github.com/AIDAVA-DEV/sulo> ;
                                           <https://schema.org/funding> \"This work is partially supported by the AIDAVA project (GA 101057062), as part of the European Union's Horizon Europe research and innovation programme.\"@en ;
                                           <https://schema.org/includedInDataCatalog> <https://lov.linkeddata.es/dataset/lov/vocabs/sulo> ;
                                           <https://w3id.org/mod#definitionProperty> rdfs:comment ;
                                           <https://w3id.org/mod#hasRepresentationLanguage> <http://omv.ontoware.org/2005/05/ontology#OWL> ;
                                           <https://w3id.org/mod#hasSyntax> <http://www.w3.org/ns/formats/Turtle> ;
                                           <https://w3id.org/mod#prefLabelProperty> rdfs:label ;
                                           <https://w3id.org/mod#status> \"active\" .\"\"\"@en .

"""@en ;
                                               skos:note "Biome numeric identifiers follow the RESOLVE biome numbering, not the order of categories in the One Earth framework article. Ecoregion and bioregion identifiers follow One Earth."@en ,
                                                         "Naming: new classes and individuals use Title_Case; new properties use lower_case; rdfs:label is the local IRI name with underscores replaced by spaces and an English language tag. Source titles are retained as dcterms:title. Ambiguous names at different hierarchy levels are disambiguated with a class-name suffix. Existing vocabulary IRIs and annotations are preserved."@en ,
                                                         "Snapshot contents: 14 Biome Type individuals, 185 Bioregion individuals, 844 Ecoregion individuals, 14 Realm individuals, 53 Subrealm individuals."@en ,
                                                         "The upper hierarchy uses has_direct_region_part and its inverse. The transitive has_region_part supports traversal through intermediate levels. Ecoregion membership uses has_ecoregion because membership can involve only part of an ecoregion. Inverse assertions are included explicitly for convenient querying without a reasoner. No geometry-derived relationships are asserted."@en .

#################################################################
#    Annotation properties
#################################################################

###  http://purl.org/dc/dcam/rangeIncludes
<http://purl.org/dc/dcam/rangeIncludes> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator
<http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty .


###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract
dcterms:abstract rdf:type owl:AnnotationProperty ;
                 rdfs:subPropertyOf dcterms:description .


###  http://purl.org/dc/terms/accessRights
